#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fail-closed isolated launcher for cross-client workflow evaluations.

This module is deliberately a *test harness*, not product runtime.  It makes
an immutable fixture copy, owns the closed client profile, and preserves raw
client/shim evidence beneath a private control root.  A normalizer may only
propose a pass after the public event-log validator accepts that external
evidence.  Until every required native and semantic adapter is available the
only safe outcome is a versioned ``incomplete`` log.

The command interface is intentionally small::

    python3 -m tests.evals.run_cross_client --client codex \
      --scenario current-wiki-fast-path --client-command-json '[...]' \
      --network-attestation workspace-egress-denied

Dynamic values use three literal, closed template slots: ``{workspace}``,
``{mcp_config}``, and ``{prompt}``.  They are accepted only in the one exact
position of the corresponding locked profile; caller paths never become
authority.
"""

